in @prism
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/lens

# @mirror/lens/shell — the interactive lens (λsh transport).
#
# The interactive transport per docs/specs/lambda-shell.md. λsh is the
# running mode of `mirror join` — "the same transport under two names";
# this shard declares the lens at the @mirror/lens family altitude.
#
# Shape (per lambda-shell.md):
#
#   λ>          computing prompt; every expression is an mq optic over
#                the graph; every pipe |> is function composition.
#   @name>      conversing prompt; a peer is present; natural language;
#                peer translates to mq internally.
#   \            toggle between computing and conversing; goes to the
#                home peer configured in the .spec.
#
# Composition shape: mq is the canonical expression language; the lens
# accepts mq verbatim. Output is mirror-text + eigenboard-colored prompt.
# History is graph: every command is a node, every result is a node,
# pipes are edges; eigenvalue ordering, not line numbers.
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Second species under @mirror/lens (after lens/cli). Transport-side
# lens: same five-operation algebra, interactive-shell audience. Per
# docs/specs/the-convergence.md §1.2: one of four transport lenses
# (cli / shell / mcp / lsp), all adapters onto the same runtime.
#
# === Body status ===
#
# FAMILY-HEADER ONLY this tick. The five-op prism block + obligation-
# blocked actions declare the shape; the bodies (the actual lambda-
# shell.md mechanics — toggle handling, peer routing, history-as-graph
# eigenvalue computation, unnamed-peer suggestion threshold) land when
# the consumer (λsh binary / `mirror join` verb) pulls. Per Last
# Responsible Moment.
#
# Cascade DEFERRED to Reed-led sweep (lambda-shell.md, the-convergence.md):
# both specs currently say `λsh`/`mirror join` as the entry pair;
# post-migration the entry verb becomes `mirror lens shell` or
# `mirror join` (depending on the cli-as-prism sub-glass surface
# Reed lands). Substrate-side declaration here is invariant under that
# choice.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/lambda-shell.md (the running-mode spec),
#               docs/specs/the-convergence.md §1 (transport recognition),
#               docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md (the `join` sub-glass that
#               enters this lens).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]].
# Related shards: lens.mirror (the family root),
#                 lens/cli.mirror, lens/mcp.mirror, lens/lsp.mirror
#                 (sibling transport lenses),
#                 lens/transit.mirror, lens/refract.mirror (sibling
#                 measurement lenses).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/lens/shell.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/lens/shell` and only that.

# === actions — abstract surface; bodies land on consumer pull ===

# enter — enter the shell. Optional peer argument; when present, the
# shell drops into `@peer>` mode (conversing). When absent, the shell
# stands in `λ>` mode (computing).
enter(peer: ref) -> shell { \ }

# toggle — the `\` keystroke. Switches between computing (λ>) and
# conversing (@home_peer>); the home peer comes from the active
# project's .spec.
toggle(s: shell) -> shell { \ }

# eval — evaluate one mq expression against the live graph; returns
# the resulting node + eigenboard-tagged prompt update.
eval(s: shell, expr: ref) -> shell { \ }

out @mirror/lens/shell
out enter
out toggle
out eval
